&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Square helps small businesses do business — operating more efficiently, selling confidently, and finding new opportunities. As our indirect sales channel scales across APAC, we need someone to own enablement for Australia outright.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a role that contributes to someone else&#39;s programme. You are the enablement function for the Australian &amp;amp; Japanese sales channel. Everything a seller in this market touches — how they&#39;re onboarded, certified, trained, coached, and measured — is yours to build, run and improve. You&#39;ll have global frameworks to draw on and a Learning Experience Designer to build with, but the decisions about what Australia needs, and the results that follow, sit with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll also extend what you build into Japan, working through our reseller and partner network. Japan is a different channel model and a different sales culture, so this is about adapting and enabling through partners rather than running the market yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role. You&#39;ll be in the field and on the phone with Independent Contractors and Channel Sales Managers, spotting performance gaps and coaching in the moment. You own the numbers, not just the calendar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We need a builder who thinks commercially — someone who creates structure from scratch, uses data to find where the biggest gains are, and gets on with it without needing much direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Australia (Sydney or Melbourne preferred), reporting into the Head of Sales Enablement, with dotted line to Head of Sales, APAC. Regular field travel within Australia and periodic travel to Japan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own enablement for Australia &amp;amp; Japan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own IC and Reseller onboarding &amp;amp; enablement strategy for the market: the programme, the content, the ramp path, and the activation numbers that come out of it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Regional Sales Manager (RSM) and Partner Manager Training &amp;amp; Certification programme — every manager properly trained, certified, and kept current&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a structured training calendar tied to commercial priorities: onboarding, product launches, regulatory change, and the capability gaps costing us revenue today&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the enablement content library (in collaboration with marketing) — sales playbooks, value selling framework, competitive insights, pricing and positioning guidance, process documentation — and make sure sellers actually use it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the single point of accountability for enablement in this market — the person Sales leadership comes to, and the person who says no when something won&#39;t move the numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring Japan&#39;s requirements into what you build for Australia early, so the second market isn&#39;t a retrofit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coaching — driving field performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RSMs in activating new ICs faster, with reporting and tracking that spots performance issues early enough to act on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data to identify your lowest and highest performers, and prioritise your coaching time where it will move the numbers most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach Channel Sales Managers directly, and run leadership programmes that improve their team&#39;s output, not just their own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give managers practical tools to run team meetings, workshops and 1:1s that translate into better team results, not just better-run meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving adoption &amp;amp; impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Channel Sales Leadership to embed enablement into everyday workflows so it shows up in the numbers, not just in a training log&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on the commercial impact of everything you own — conversion, activation, ramp time, retention — and use that data to double down on what&#39;s working and cut what isn&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align readiness plans with Product and Marketing so sellers are fully productive from day one of a launch, not weeks behind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed what works in APAC back into the global enablement model, and pull in what&#39;s working elsewhere rather than rebuilding it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for the connection between enablement and channel sales performance — this role is measured on results, not activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in sales enablement, sales coaching, sales training or similar — ideally in a high-growth or channel-driven environment, with a track record of moving performance metrics, not just delivering training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning enablement for a market or business unit, not just running programmes inside someone else&#39;s — you&#39;ve set the priorities and carried the results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real field coaching experience — you&#39;ve actually developed salespeople directly and can point to the results it drove (conversion, deal size, ramp time, retention)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder mindset with a commercial edge — you&#39;ve created structure and programmes from scratch, and you judge success by the numbers they produced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong content design and facilitation skills, with training you&#39;ve built that sellers actually use and that shows up in performance data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to turn complex information into clear, simple frameworks and messaging that sellers can apply immediately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management, especially across Sales, Product and Marketing, and the confidence to hold a position with senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuinely analytical mindset — you&#39;re comfortable in performance data, spotting the gaps that matter and proving impact after the fact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating across cultures, with the judgement to know when to standardise and when to build something market-specific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Business-level Japanese an advantage&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel regularly within Australia and periodically to Japan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: fintech, payments or POS experience; familiarity with Australian SME sales cycles; experience with reseller, distributor or independent channel models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Guidelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may submit up to 9 active applications within a 60-day period. Reapplications to the same role are accepted 90 days after a previous application has been reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We may use automated AI tools to evaluate job applications for efficiency and consistency. These tools comply with local regulations, including bias audits, and we handle all personal data in accordance with state and local privacy laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact us &lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.block.xyz/privacyportal/form&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;with hiring practice or data usage questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Every benefit we offer is designed with one goal: empowering you to do the best work of your career while building the life you want. Remote work, medical insurance, flexible time off, retirement savings plans, and modern family planning are just some of our offering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://block.xyz/employee-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://block.xyz/documents/benefits.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Check out our other benefits at Block.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Block, Inc. (NYSE: XYZ) builds technology to increase access to the global economy. Each of our brands unlocks different aspects of the economy for more people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Square&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;makes commerce and financial services accessible to sellers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Cash App&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the easy way to spend, send, and store money.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Afterpay&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is transforming the way customers manage their spending over time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;TIDAL&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a music platform that empowers artists to thrive as entrepreneurs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Bitkey&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a simple self-custody wallet built for bitcoin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Proto&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a suite of bitcoin mining products and services. Together, we’re helping build a financial system that is open to everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
